1
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:19,720
(Jung Yong Hwa)

2
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:22,730
(Hong Seung Hee)

3
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:26,200
(Lee Yi Kyung)

4
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:29,330
(Park Yu Na)

5
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:44,050
(Oh! My Guard)

6
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:45,280
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

7
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:47,250
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:52,220
Do not touch that!

9
00:00:55,530 --> 00:00:56,530
You startled me.

10
00:01:05,865 --> 00:01:07,535
Why did you barge into someone else's room?

11
00:01:08,875 --> 00:01:09,875
That...

12
00:01:11,435 --> 00:01:12,905
That's not something you can just touch.

13
00:01:14,175 --> 00:01:16,305
No, I was just...

14
00:01:17,801 --> 00:01:18,801
Get out.

15
00:01:23,531 --> 00:01:25,371
(Kim Jae Hee's)

16
00:01:47,831 --> 00:01:50,131
The things the young lady collected here...

17
00:01:50,131 --> 00:01:51,531
Oh, those.

18
00:01:51,631 --> 00:01:54,271
Earlier today, Secretary Kim told me to clear them all out.

19
00:01:54,371 --> 00:01:56,431
I didn't throw them away. I put them in the basement.

20
00:02:07,811 --> 00:02:09,311
You're in a killer mood.

21
00:02:09,911 --> 00:02:11,851
Hong Du must have caused some trouble again.

22
00:02:17,161 --> 00:02:20,091
No. I was trying to find the bathroom...

23
00:02:20,461 --> 00:02:22,661
I didn't mean to go into that room.

24
00:02:22,895 --> 00:02:23,895
That room?

25
00:02:27,365 --> 00:02:28,405
Into your daughter's room...

26
00:02:29,305 --> 00:02:31,135
We went into your daughter's room. I'm sorry.

27
00:02:32,005 --> 00:02:33,305
His daughter's room?

28
00:02:43,785 --> 00:02:44,815
It's fine.

29
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:49,755
See? He says it's fine.

30
00:02:55,565 --> 00:02:58,995
Chairman, your invitation today...

31
00:02:59,065 --> 00:03:01,005
was a tremendous honour.

32
00:03:02,165 --> 00:03:04,075
- From now on, often... - I will invite you often.

33
00:03:04,135 --> 00:03:06,505
Yes. We'll be going now.

34
00:03:06,635 --> 00:03:08,405
- Thank you. - Yes.

35
00:03:15,285 --> 00:03:16,315
Then...

36
00:03:21,025 --> 00:03:22,125
Are you satisfied?

37
00:03:22,925 --> 00:03:25,395
Even after the young lady came home, you confirmed...

38
00:03:26,655 --> 00:03:27,965
she doesn't remember anything, right?

39
00:03:30,635 --> 00:03:31,795
Did Hae Ra...

40
00:03:34,365 --> 00:03:36,365
always have so many expressions?

41
00:03:48,485 --> 00:03:52,185
Now tell me, why was BK off-limits today?

42
00:03:52,455 --> 00:03:54,185
And why couldn't we say he was the chairman there?

43
00:03:54,425 --> 00:03:55,455
That's because...

44
00:03:56,255 --> 00:03:59,525
The Chairman is so secretive, he doesn't like revealing that.

45
00:04:00,465 --> 00:04:02,325
- CEO Park, you're suspicious. - Right.

46
00:04:02,395 --> 00:04:05,665
It feels like you're hiding a secret all to yourself.

47
00:04:05,665 --> 00:04:06,795
My gosh.

48
00:04:06,935 --> 00:04:09,435
I have absolutely nothing to be ashamed of.

49
00:04:09,505 --> 00:04:11,005
Of course, there might be a little something...

50
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:13,135
What? What, why are you looking at me like that?

51
00:04:13,205 --> 00:04:16,205
- What? Why? - But did you see the way...

52
00:04:16,345 --> 00:04:17,615
the Chairman looked at Hong Du earlier?

53
00:04:17,675 --> 00:04:20,545
It was, like, really profound.

54
00:04:21,145 --> 00:04:22,715
Like he was looking at his lost daughter.

55
00:04:23,415 --> 00:04:25,185
- What daughter? - Yes.

56
00:04:25,315 --> 00:04:27,085
And what about the way he looked at you...

57
00:04:27,325 --> 00:04:30,525
If you came home late drinking, I said I'd kill you, remember?

58
00:04:30,595 --> 00:04:34,565
And I'd kill anyone who sent you home late, too.

59
00:04:34,625 --> 00:04:36,525
I'll definitely keep my promise.

60
00:04:36,595 --> 00:04:39,795
If you make my daughter cry, you're all dead.

61
00:04:40,395 --> 00:04:42,665
If you make Cha Hong Du cry, he'll just...

62
00:04:42,735 --> 00:04:45,875
wipe us all out. Especially you.

63
00:04:46,705 --> 00:04:48,975
I mean, he was looking at Tae Bong...

64
00:04:49,045 --> 00:04:50,475
like a potential son-in-law.

65
00:04:51,015 --> 00:04:52,915
- Son-in-law? - Yes.

66
00:04:52,975 --> 00:04:54,515
Oh, my.

67
00:04:56,685 --> 00:04:58,915
- You have a sixth sense, do you? - I do?

68
00:04:58,985 --> 00:05:01,325
How about me? Do you see wealth in my future?

69
00:05:01,385 --> 00:05:03,655
Will I die counting money? What do you think?

70
00:05:10,665 --> 00:05:11,665
Oh. You are here?

71
00:05:11,935 --> 00:05:13,095
You are here?

72
00:05:14,535 --> 00:05:17,335
What is wrong with him now? Father, I am going to leave now.

73
00:05:18,305 --> 00:05:19,735
- I am leaving. - Thank you.

74
00:05:19,805 --> 00:05:21,805
Did Father give you a hard time or...

75
00:05:21,805 --> 00:05:22,975
It was not hard at all.

76
00:05:22,975 --> 00:05:24,245
Come by the restaurant with him sometime.

77
00:05:25,175 --> 00:05:26,215
Thank you.

78
00:05:38,125 --> 00:05:41,725
I am bored. Play with me.

79
00:05:42,795 --> 00:05:44,635
That guy from earlier would not play with me.

80
00:05:46,165 --> 00:05:47,235
I will play with you.

81
00:05:53,205 --> 00:05:54,805
When you smile like that...

82
00:05:56,345 --> 00:05:57,715
You are pretty when you smile.

83
00:06:01,585 --> 00:06:04,785
You sound just like him, sir.

84
00:06:05,955 --> 00:06:06,955
Min Seok.

85
00:06:07,485 --> 00:06:08,685
Min Seok?

86
00:06:12,655 --> 00:06:16,625
The person I am thankful for, who left on a warm day.

87
00:06:23,565 --> 00:06:24,635
That is right.

88
00:06:24,635 --> 00:06:26,505
Someone I am thankful for, just like your wife, sir.

89
00:06:28,045 --> 00:06:29,045
Someone I am thankful for.

90
00:06:36,245 --> 00:06:37,615
You should not force a smile.

91
00:06:41,325 --> 00:06:43,055
If you force a smile,

92
00:06:44,025 --> 00:06:45,655
it gets dark in here.

93
00:06:46,355 --> 00:06:48,825
When it gets dark in here,

94
00:06:49,465 --> 00:06:52,195
my hands become healing hands.

95
00:07:05,445 --> 00:07:06,815
I can see everything without even looking.

96
00:07:09,445 --> 00:07:11,285
You must have been in so much pain.

97
00:07:18,425 --> 00:07:19,955
You will be all better now.

98
00:07:21,395 --> 00:07:23,465
Because I am doing this.

99
00:07:25,735 --> 00:07:26,965
Doing this for you.

100
00:07:31,235 --> 00:07:32,275
Actually...

101
00:07:33,235 --> 00:07:34,675
after that child died,

102
00:07:38,315 --> 00:07:40,275
I had never smiled properly.

103
00:07:43,645 --> 00:07:44,685
And because of that,

104
00:07:45,985 --> 00:07:48,085
I forgot how to truly smile.

105
00:07:49,425 --> 00:07:51,495
And a guy like that wanted to become an actor.

106
00:07:52,995 --> 00:07:54,925
Even I think it is crazy.

107
00:07:56,665 --> 00:07:58,265
But he held onto me,

108
00:08:00,235 --> 00:08:02,235
and Min Seok taught me every day.

109
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:06,005
How to force a smile.

110
00:08:09,745 --> 00:08:10,745
But...

111
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:14,315
The place I went to today...

112
00:08:18,485 --> 00:08:19,785
was that child's house.

113
00:08:23,025 --> 00:08:24,595
In that child's former home,

114
00:08:29,295 --> 00:08:30,765
I am not supposed to smile.

115
00:08:34,265 --> 00:08:35,435
That house?

116
00:08:40,235 --> 00:08:41,905
Then the Chairman's daughter...

117
00:08:43,105 --> 00:08:44,245
is dead?

118
00:08:52,915 --> 00:08:54,485
Because he missed her so much.

119
00:08:57,085 --> 00:08:58,725
Because he can never see her again.

120
00:09:02,995 --> 00:09:04,365
That is why he did that.

121
00:09:07,765 --> 00:09:08,805
The Chairman, too.

122
00:09:21,385 --> 00:09:24,285
But why does that place feel so familiar to me? Why?

123
00:09:40,195 --> 00:09:44,805
Please tell me. Is Cha Hong Du really Oh Hae Ra?

124
00:09:45,475 --> 00:09:48,175
You seem very interested in the owner's family, Director Han.

125
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:49,845
You are not denying it.

126
00:09:50,815 --> 00:09:53,015
And what is the name of this person with no boyfriend?

127
00:09:53,215 --> 00:09:54,915
- Cha Hong Du. - Cha Hong Du...

128
00:09:55,045 --> 00:09:58,355
But I know she's completely different from you, Hong Du.

129
00:09:58,455 --> 00:09:59,955
Completely different from me?

130
00:10:00,015 --> 00:10:03,325
- Then you must be Oh Hae Ra. - Oh Hae Ra? Who is that?

131
00:10:05,255 --> 00:10:06,295
But...

132
00:10:07,895 --> 00:10:09,395
You are saying you are that Oh Hae Ra?

133
00:10:21,205 --> 00:10:24,005
That's not something you can just touch.

134
00:10:32,785 --> 00:10:36,025
(Kim Jae Hee's)

135
00:10:40,395 --> 00:10:41,395
Young lady.

136
00:10:41,465 --> 00:10:43,325
I hate the name written here. I hate it.

137
00:10:43,495 --> 00:10:44,495
I'm going to throw it away.

138
00:12:03,205 --> 00:12:05,475
Who are you? I'm sure you are not a fan of mine.

139
00:12:07,785 --> 00:12:09,985
Well, the thing is...

140
00:12:09,985 --> 00:12:12,785
You have been watching me, the people around me,

141
00:12:12,855 --> 00:12:14,825
and even around my house for a long time.

142
00:12:14,955 --> 00:12:18,595
I have been watching you too.

143
00:12:22,065 --> 00:12:24,195
Well, about that...

144
00:12:24,265 --> 00:12:26,995
February 9, living together under the same roof...

145
00:12:27,805 --> 00:12:29,465
No, I mean, started the live-in arrangement.

146
00:12:29,635 --> 00:12:31,175
It's 3,000 dollars a month. Once her probation ends,

147
00:12:31,235 --> 00:12:32,235
I'll raise it.

148
00:12:32,375 --> 00:12:35,145
And I covered all the travel expenses too.

149
00:12:39,115 --> 00:12:41,915
Currently, she is calling someone who is not her father her father.

150
00:12:42,015 --> 00:12:43,785
Sometimes she is in danger because of a stalker...

151
00:12:43,985 --> 00:12:45,985
Oh, I will take care of that for sure as well.

152
00:12:46,055 --> 00:12:48,285
From now on, I'll take her to the hospital too...

153
00:12:48,455 --> 00:12:52,655
and buy her nice clothes. What else is there?

154
00:12:53,055 --> 00:12:56,325
Why are you telling me all this...

155
00:12:58,135 --> 00:12:59,235
Because you are Cha Hong Du's...

156
00:13:00,435 --> 00:13:01,565
father.

157
00:13:08,845 --> 00:13:13,015
I have an eye for these things, I recognised it at first sight.

158
00:13:13,015 --> 00:13:14,315
That you are Cha Hong Du's father.

159
00:13:15,015 --> 00:13:18,315
Those fierce eyes, that chilling aura...

160
00:13:18,915 --> 00:13:21,055
People must have told you...

161
00:13:21,125 --> 00:13:22,655
that intimidating aura is a dead ringer for hers, right?

162
00:13:23,025 --> 00:13:24,025
Excuse me?

163
00:13:26,325 --> 00:13:29,965
- No, that is not it. I am... - Do not worry.

164
00:13:31,465 --> 00:13:33,665
I do not know what happened in the past.

165
00:13:34,635 --> 00:13:37,875
But your daughter, I will take good care of her.

166
00:13:38,335 --> 00:13:40,335
However, the doctor said...

167
00:13:40,675 --> 00:13:42,705
if she has to take in too much all at once,

168
00:13:43,175 --> 00:13:44,575
things could get so heated up in here...

169
00:13:45,015 --> 00:13:46,545
that she might just break down.

170
00:13:47,515 --> 00:13:49,985
So for now, please just...

171
00:13:50,885 --> 00:13:52,785
watch over her slowly from a distance.

172
00:13:54,785 --> 00:13:56,085
She's loved.

173
00:13:57,725 --> 00:13:58,725
Pardon?

174
00:14:00,595 --> 00:14:01,895
I will do that.

175
00:14:02,625 --> 00:14:05,265
Very slowly, from a distance.

176
00:14:06,435 --> 00:14:07,435
Thank you.

177
00:14:07,705 --> 00:14:08,765
By any chance,

178
00:14:09,965 --> 00:14:12,305
have we met before?

179
00:14:15,745 --> 00:14:17,915
Sir, if you do not know who I am,

180
00:14:18,115 --> 00:14:20,045
people will say you are behind the times.

181
00:14:20,115 --> 00:14:23,745
I am a famous guy. But still,

182
00:14:24,185 --> 00:14:25,255
I will do my best.

183
00:14:26,655 --> 00:14:27,655
Yes.

184
00:14:28,555 --> 00:14:30,955
But have you ever lived in Seoul?

185
00:14:31,595 --> 00:14:33,595
Perhaps when you were very young.

186
00:14:35,025 --> 00:14:36,025
Pardon?

187
00:14:36,895 --> 00:14:38,465
Is Um Tae Bong...

188
00:14:39,765 --> 00:14:43,405
(Kim Jae Hee's)

189
00:14:43,865 --> 00:14:45,005
your real name?

190
00:14:50,105 --> 00:14:52,215
Is this how a father with a daughter feels?

191
00:14:52,775 --> 00:14:55,985
Still, we should do the interview properly later.

192
00:14:56,515 --> 00:14:58,155
Take care on your way back.

193
00:15:00,555 --> 00:15:02,625
- I will get going. - Okay.

194
00:15:04,825 --> 00:15:07,125
- Get home safely. - Yes.

195
00:15:15,305 --> 00:15:16,535
It really cannot be him.

196
00:15:40,755 --> 00:15:42,125
I was going to give this to him.

197
00:15:43,895 --> 00:15:46,535
It is just a cameo, so it is not important.

198
00:15:46,535 --> 00:15:47,565
Understood.

199
00:15:49,335 --> 00:15:50,335
Hey.

200
00:15:50,405 --> 00:15:52,305
(Cha Hong Du)

201
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:57,475
What are you staring at?

202
00:15:57,775 --> 00:15:58,775
I was not looking.

203
00:15:58,845 --> 00:16:01,075
You were staring, and now you are lying.

204
00:16:01,685 --> 00:16:03,985
- Hey. - Cut it out.

205
00:16:04,185 --> 00:16:05,455
I already caused a scene inside.

206
00:16:08,155 --> 00:16:09,155
Hey.

207
00:16:10,685 --> 00:16:11,755
Do you have a light?

208
00:16:13,255 --> 00:16:15,465
Darn it, who told you to hit her with my shoe?

209
00:16:15,525 --> 00:16:16,525
Mom, she is...

210
00:16:16,595 --> 00:16:18,495
hitting Hong Du in the head with my sneaker again.

211
00:16:18,735 --> 00:16:20,735
Darn it. I told you not to curse at me.

212
00:16:20,795 --> 00:16:22,265
Then you should not have used my sneaker to hit her.

213
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:25,775
- Are you even listening to me? - Hey. Let go.

214
00:16:25,835 --> 00:16:27,305
- Are you going to let go? - Let go.

215
00:16:27,375 --> 00:16:29,345
- You let go. - How dare you grab my hair.

216
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:30,405
I said you let go too.

217
00:16:30,475 --> 00:16:32,475
- Let go, you let go first. - Let go on the count of three.

218
00:16:32,545 --> 00:16:33,875
- One, two, - One, two,

219
00:16:34,015 --> 00:16:35,045
- Three. - Three.

220
00:16:35,645 --> 00:16:36,845
Mom.

221
00:16:37,545 --> 00:16:38,555
(Police)

222
00:16:39,155 --> 00:16:40,155
Darn it.

223
00:16:40,785 --> 00:16:42,285
Um Tae Bong, here.

224
00:16:43,255 --> 00:16:44,255
You startled me.

225
00:16:48,525 --> 00:16:49,865
Let's go to the restroom.

226
00:16:50,625 --> 00:16:51,695
Hurry.

227
00:16:52,265 --> 00:16:54,765
What are you talking about? Replace the cameo actor...

228
00:16:54,835 --> 00:16:56,065
with someone else now?

229
00:16:56,135 --> 00:16:57,365
And on the day of the shoot, no less.

230
00:16:57,565 --> 00:16:59,335
I am begging you.

231
00:16:59,405 --> 00:17:01,605
She is back on camera for the first time in three years.

232
00:17:01,675 --> 00:17:04,515
She has reflected enough, so please give her a chance.

233
00:17:04,575 --> 00:17:06,345
I heard you two worked on a project together before.

234
00:17:06,415 --> 00:17:09,145
Just go with someone else.

235
00:17:09,715 --> 00:17:11,415
I'm a professional director in this industry.

236
00:17:11,485 --> 00:17:12,755
The final casting decision is mine...

237
00:17:12,815 --> 00:17:13,855
We dated.

238
00:17:14,755 --> 00:17:16,155
We dated,

239
00:17:16,885 --> 00:17:18,195
but she dumped me.

240
00:17:18,795 --> 00:17:21,265
This jerk is even going after married women now...

241
00:17:21,965 --> 00:17:25,335
Seriously. What kind of jerk is this?

242
00:17:25,695 --> 00:17:28,235
Director Kim, how can you do this?

243
00:17:28,305 --> 00:17:29,305
Standby. Where is the AD?

244
00:17:29,365 --> 00:17:31,065
- I can really do a good job. - We are losing the light.

245
00:17:34,105 --> 00:17:35,175
All right, standby.

246
00:17:35,805 --> 00:17:37,205
(Restricted Area)

247
00:17:40,145 --> 00:17:41,815
Where is Cha Hong Du?

248
00:17:41,885 --> 00:17:43,645
She left in a hurry earlier after getting a call from CEO Park.

249
00:17:43,715 --> 00:17:45,155
She said she would explain it to you later.

250
00:17:45,485 --> 00:17:47,055
She should have told me she was leaving.

251
00:17:47,485 --> 00:17:49,325
Why are you taking care of the costumes?

252
00:17:49,385 --> 00:17:51,525
Does she think she is a real stylist or something?

253
00:17:52,095 --> 00:17:53,125
Darn it.

254
00:17:55,295 --> 00:17:56,295
He is really going to...

255
00:17:56,365 --> 00:17:58,095
have to learn his lesson the hard way.

256
00:17:58,735 --> 00:17:59,735
(Ten Dollars)

257
00:18:02,035 --> 00:18:03,635
I have got front row seats for this.

258
00:18:06,975 --> 00:18:08,675
Hey, what was with that wink?

259
00:18:10,805 --> 00:18:11,975
I am really sorry.

260
00:18:14,075 --> 00:18:17,385
That is why dementia patients require special attention,

261
00:18:17,745 --> 00:18:20,955
and as I mentioned last time, once they enter the middle stages,

262
00:18:21,015 --> 00:18:23,085
living in a nursing home with specialised care...

263
00:18:23,725 --> 00:18:26,155
is a much better environment for the patient.

264
00:18:28,295 --> 00:18:30,825
- Father. - Yes?

265
00:18:33,035 --> 00:18:34,865
Father, over here.

266
00:18:43,905 --> 00:18:45,775
Is there anything you want to do, Father?

267
00:18:46,415 --> 00:18:47,575
Anyone you want to see?

268
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:52,915
My wife.

269
00:18:55,185 --> 00:18:56,225
My daughter.

270
00:18:59,655 --> 00:19:01,095
Where could they be?

271
00:19:11,975 --> 00:19:13,235
Tae Bong.

272
00:19:13,835 --> 00:19:16,205
It is something you have to go through eventually.

273
00:19:16,645 --> 00:19:19,075
I cannot stay by his side all the time either.

274
00:19:19,145 --> 00:19:20,375
It is bleeding, darn it.

275
00:19:20,775 --> 00:19:24,015
Let us just think about what is best for him, okay?

276
00:19:24,855 --> 00:19:26,155
I will look into hospitals.

277
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:31,425
Cha Hong Du will never agree to it.

278
00:19:31,495 --> 00:19:34,525
I will somehow try to persuade her myself.

279
00:19:35,495 --> 00:19:36,495
Listen.

280
00:19:40,665 --> 00:19:42,735
Let us send Father to a nursing hospital.

281
00:19:45,335 --> 00:19:47,705
We have been too much of a burden on CEO Park.

282
00:19:48,505 --> 00:19:50,605
It would be better for Father's sake, too.

283
00:19:53,575 --> 00:19:57,015
Our Hong Du is so mature for her age...

284
00:19:57,485 --> 00:19:59,685
Right? Isn't she?

285
00:20:00,215 --> 00:20:01,555
Before he goes to the nursing home,

286
00:20:01,685 --> 00:20:03,225
tell me everything you want to do for him.

287
00:20:05,155 --> 00:20:08,395
There is actually one thing.

288
00:20:10,025 --> 00:20:12,335
No, it is fine if I do not meet them.

289
00:20:16,905 --> 00:20:18,335
"It is fine if I do not meet them?"

290
00:20:20,105 --> 00:20:23,175
Hey, no way. Do not even think about it.

291
00:20:23,605 --> 00:20:25,775
Whatever just popped into your head, I am against it.

292
00:20:31,585 --> 00:20:33,955
Yes, I'm that popular right now.

293
00:20:34,155 --> 00:20:35,825
How many times have I been number one in search trends?

294
00:20:36,325 --> 00:20:39,355
Every drama I filmed became a hit. The Traitors of Huam-dong,

295
00:20:39,425 --> 00:20:40,955
Your Mister, Office Romance,

296
00:20:41,025 --> 00:20:42,695
and what was that one starring Kim Man Gil...

297
00:20:43,165 --> 00:20:44,165
Passionate Bride.

298
00:20:45,195 --> 00:20:46,535
Right, so no more of those rough roles...

299
00:20:46,595 --> 00:20:49,705
where I am cursing and acting all vulgar.

300
00:20:49,965 --> 00:20:51,435
You know, the kind of role where I deliver a line...

301
00:20:51,475 --> 00:20:53,205
and it feels like flower petals are falling from my lips,

302
00:20:53,275 --> 00:20:54,535
with a sweet fragrance floating in the air...

303
00:20:54,605 --> 00:20:55,605
That kind of role.

304
00:20:56,375 --> 00:20:58,545
- Who is it? - Should I tell them to come in?

305
00:20:59,375 --> 00:21:01,445
- Yes. - Please come in.

306
00:21:01,515 --> 00:21:03,615
I am only going to do roles like that, you get the vibe?

307
00:21:07,785 --> 00:21:10,085
Those sisters you were looking for, Hong Du,

308
00:21:10,525 --> 00:21:13,525
I found all of them, because of a certain someone.

309
00:21:14,295 --> 00:21:17,195
Really? Thank you so much. Thank you.

310
00:21:17,265 --> 00:21:20,165
- It is nothing. - That is CEO Park for you.

311
00:21:20,335 --> 00:21:22,165
See? You can do it if you try.

312
00:21:22,465 --> 00:21:23,465
You punk.

313
00:21:24,935 --> 00:21:28,345
But Hong Du, about your stepmother.

314
00:21:28,645 --> 00:21:32,645
I could not meet her in person, but I heard some news.

315
00:21:33,645 --> 00:21:34,715
Where was it again?

316
00:21:34,785 --> 00:21:37,485
Anyway, she is overseas, and it is too far away,

317
00:21:37,585 --> 00:21:38,985
so she says she cannot come.

318
00:21:41,085 --> 00:21:45,695
That's fine. I'm just relieved to be seeing my sisters again.

319
00:21:46,855 --> 00:21:48,965
- I am sorry. - Thank you.

320
00:21:49,595 --> 00:21:51,765
I am tired.

321
00:22:04,575 --> 00:22:06,145
It has been a long time.

322
00:22:07,475 --> 00:22:10,185
I know. It really has been a while, right?

323
00:22:13,315 --> 00:22:16,085
I am sorry. I am just so happy to see you.

324
00:22:17,855 --> 00:22:19,055
So that is what happened.

325
00:22:19,755 --> 00:22:21,825
About me fighting my mother-in-law on that variety show,

326
00:22:21,895 --> 00:22:23,395
the director called me every morning at dawn,

327
00:22:23,465 --> 00:22:26,935
and the writer kept telling me to make it entertaining...

328
00:22:27,135 --> 00:22:29,335
Right. That is how all variety shows work.

329
00:22:32,505 --> 00:22:34,075
What about your nose?

330
00:22:34,135 --> 00:22:35,975
I became so unlikeable because of that,

331
00:22:36,045 --> 00:22:37,605
so I could not film a drama for years.

332
00:22:37,675 --> 00:22:39,275
I barely managed to get a cameo appearance.

333
00:22:39,875 --> 00:22:40,875
And then...

334
00:22:41,115 --> 00:22:45,655
- Um Tae Bong criticised me again. - That punk Tae Bong...

335
00:22:45,715 --> 00:22:46,755
What a jerk.

336
00:22:46,915 --> 00:22:51,325
Anyway, my point is, as a way to apologize,

337
00:22:51,755 --> 00:22:54,055
he wants you to join the fan event...

338
00:22:54,755 --> 00:22:57,325
that Tae Bong prepared. That is what I am saying.

339
00:22:57,465 --> 00:22:58,465
What do you think?

340
00:22:59,165 --> 00:23:00,465
What do I have to do?

341
00:23:03,705 --> 00:23:04,735
Well...

342
00:23:05,105 --> 00:23:06,275
Please do not cry.

343
00:23:08,645 --> 00:23:11,545
But you have changed so much from before.

344
00:23:12,675 --> 00:23:13,675
I am sorry.

345
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:16,315
I am sorry that I have changed so much.

346
00:23:16,845 --> 00:23:20,085
No, I did not mean it like that.

347
00:23:23,725 --> 00:23:28,365
But you also seem to have changed a lot.

348
00:23:29,195 --> 00:23:30,195
Really?

349
00:23:31,795 --> 00:23:32,965
You have too.

350
00:23:35,065 --> 00:23:37,365
I am sorry, CEO Park. I left the entertainment industry...

351
00:23:37,435 --> 00:23:39,035
after that drama ended, but more importantly,

352
00:23:39,105 --> 00:23:43,245
since I received the General, I break out in hives if I lie.

353
00:23:48,685 --> 00:23:49,685
Here.

354
00:23:53,155 --> 00:23:56,285
Man, I really want you to do this. Here, here. Double.

355
00:23:57,125 --> 00:23:59,395
I understand your situation,

356
00:23:59,725 --> 00:24:02,195
but I only listen to the General's voice now.

357
00:24:03,225 --> 00:24:05,435
Yes, he says he will write you a talisman,

358
00:24:05,935 --> 00:24:07,135
so take it with you when you leave.

359
00:24:07,195 --> 00:24:09,435
One, two, three. I shook it!

360
00:24:09,505 --> 00:24:10,505
Okay.

361
00:24:10,865 --> 00:24:12,975
Well, the General is saying "okay."

362
00:24:13,675 --> 00:24:16,845
But if the General suddenly comes out,

363
00:24:17,845 --> 00:24:18,945
I cannot take responsibility.

364
00:24:23,445 --> 00:24:26,385
- Has it been 1 year? - Not 1 year, but 6 years.

365
00:24:26,485 --> 00:24:28,385
The year Cha Hong Du turned 22,

366
00:24:28,485 --> 00:24:30,425
you all fled in the middle of the night and left her behind.

367
00:24:30,655 --> 00:24:33,155
No, that's not right.

368
00:24:33,295 --> 00:24:35,795
It is really great to see you after six years.

369
00:24:36,025 --> 00:24:37,995
I am so happy to see you that I could crap my pants.

370
00:24:42,305 --> 00:24:44,165
Have you been okay? Have you been well?

371
00:24:45,205 --> 00:24:47,435
Now, the concept is not being happy to see her.

372
00:24:47,575 --> 00:24:48,875
You should not be too nice, either.

373
00:24:49,475 --> 00:24:50,875
I acted too friendly, did I not?

374
00:24:51,545 --> 00:24:53,145
I acted too nice, right?

375
00:24:53,215 --> 00:24:56,615
- I am sorry. What should I do? - It is fine.

376
00:24:56,915 --> 00:24:59,855
- Please stop crying. - Second sister, your line.

377
00:25:01,215 --> 00:25:02,225
By the way,

378
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:06,495
how have you been?

379
00:25:15,565 --> 00:25:17,535
- What is it? - I see it.

380
00:25:18,875 --> 00:25:19,905
I see it.

381
00:25:21,975 --> 00:25:24,675
How did you end up losing your mind?

382
00:25:29,085 --> 00:25:30,845
What are you doing right now?

383
00:25:31,185 --> 00:25:32,785
There is a sound coming from your ear...

384
00:25:32,855 --> 00:25:33,855
What?

385
00:25:34,585 --> 00:25:35,585
Why?

386
00:25:37,855 --> 00:25:39,355
- Nonsense. - Yes.

387
00:25:39,825 --> 00:25:41,125
What are you laughing at?

388
00:25:41,495 --> 00:25:44,295
- Nonsense. Nonsense. - At this rate,

389
00:25:44,892 --> 00:25:45,892
I think we are going to get caught.

390
00:25:45,962 --> 00:25:47,532
That is why I told you not to do this from the beginning.

391
00:25:47,592 --> 00:25:48,662
If they confess that it is all fake,

392
00:25:48,732 --> 00:25:50,102
- It is hot. - what are you going to do?

393
00:25:50,232 --> 00:25:51,772
I will go over there and sort it out.

394
00:25:51,832 --> 00:25:52,902
I will go right now.

395
00:25:53,232 --> 00:25:54,432
Excuse me, did we order?

396
00:25:54,602 --> 00:25:56,372
- Wait a second. - What should we eat?

397
00:25:57,302 --> 00:25:59,412
What is going on? Is that person an actor too?

398
00:25:59,472 --> 00:26:01,142
- This is really weird. - Right?

399
00:26:01,342 --> 00:26:03,642
A drama from three years ago, how am I supposed to remember that?

400
00:26:03,712 --> 00:26:05,612
I do not even remember my lines or my name.

401
00:26:08,082 --> 00:26:11,652
What an absolute load of nonsense. Total nonsense. You little brat.

402
00:26:12,392 --> 00:26:14,622
- Right, you... - What? You...

403
00:26:14,692 --> 00:26:17,022
Just because I fed and supported your dad all this time,

404
00:26:17,092 --> 00:26:18,892
are you acting all high and mighty with me?

405
00:26:19,432 --> 00:26:20,632
You little brat.

406
00:26:22,502 --> 00:26:25,132
- It is hot. - Stepmother?

407
00:26:25,932 --> 00:26:27,372
Yes, I'm your stepmother.

408
00:26:29,342 --> 00:26:32,072
So why did you want to see me?

409
00:26:33,912 --> 00:26:35,282
I am sick of this.

410
00:26:35,912 --> 00:26:38,082
If I had sold the house and run away instead of just taking the deposit,

411
00:26:38,142 --> 00:26:40,482
you would have put me on the news, would you not? You would have.

412
00:26:42,452 --> 00:26:43,852
Hey, brats, why are you not greeting your mother...

413
00:26:43,922 --> 00:26:44,982
when you see her?

414
00:26:47,852 --> 00:26:50,622
Ma'am, this is weird. Are we really doing a fan event?

415
00:26:50,962 --> 00:26:51,962
They said this is some kind of...

416
00:26:52,032 --> 00:26:54,692
"We will make you Cha Hong Du" event winner,

417
00:26:54,762 --> 00:26:55,932
but her immersion is insane.

418
00:26:56,662 --> 00:26:59,132
I get it already, just shut up and follow my lead.

419
00:26:59,132 --> 00:27:00,972
I will explain it to you in detail later.

420
00:27:04,302 --> 00:27:07,972
Why are you glaring at me with those big, round eyes of yours?

421
00:27:08,212 --> 00:27:09,242
What? Are you shocked...

422
00:27:09,312 --> 00:27:11,982
that everyone you wished were dead all showed up at once?

423
00:27:12,152 --> 00:27:15,182
- Surprise. - That is what it is, right?

424
00:27:15,252 --> 00:27:16,982
That is why she is glaring at us like that.

425
00:27:17,482 --> 00:27:18,992
Exactly. If you keep that up,

426
00:27:19,292 --> 00:27:20,392
you are going to get beaten to death...

427
00:27:20,452 --> 00:27:22,122
by Mom and that witch of a sister.

428
00:27:22,562 --> 00:27:24,892
Hey! How dare you call your older sister that?

429
00:27:24,962 --> 00:27:26,692
You have to act like an older sister to be treated like one.

430
00:27:26,762 --> 00:27:28,292
- You little... - Are you going to hit me?

431
00:27:28,632 --> 00:27:30,062
Do I have to rip your hair out for you to wake up?

432
00:27:30,132 --> 00:27:33,272
- Mom, make her stop. - Hey, be quiet.

433
00:27:33,572 --> 00:27:34,572
Let go.

434
00:27:34,872 --> 00:27:36,142
- Let go. - Let go.

435
00:27:37,272 --> 00:27:40,472
Anyway, whenever these witches meet, all they do is fight.

436
00:27:41,312 --> 00:27:42,982
So why did you want to see me?

437
00:27:43,042 --> 00:27:46,312
What? Did you miss your stepmother's curses?

438
00:27:47,752 --> 00:27:48,752
Yes.

439
00:27:50,222 --> 00:27:51,822
I really wanted to hear it.

440
00:27:53,122 --> 00:27:54,422
Should we go right now?

441
00:28:02,062 --> 00:28:05,772
Tae Bong. Honey, I am Jung Yeong Ju.

442
00:28:05,832 --> 00:28:08,232
Jung Yeong Ju. You know me.

443
00:28:08,302 --> 00:28:10,702
The epitome of elegance and steadfastness.

444
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:12,972
But what are you asking someone like me to do now?

445
00:28:15,812 --> 00:28:17,182
Just because an actor got a little famous,

446
00:28:17,242 --> 00:28:18,982
should they be picky about their roles?

447
00:28:20,212 --> 00:28:21,382
What are you doing right now?

448
00:28:24,222 --> 00:28:25,692
That is what you used to say.

449
00:28:26,252 --> 00:28:28,252
The passion and confidence you showed...

450
00:28:28,322 --> 00:28:29,992
on various stages and screens.

451
00:28:30,062 --> 00:28:32,862
As a fellow actor, it always warmed my heart.

452
00:28:33,162 --> 00:28:36,002
Ma'am, I am asking you one more time.

453
00:28:38,462 --> 00:28:41,402
Why are you praising me so aggressively?

454
00:28:41,472 --> 00:28:42,742
It is embarrassing.

455
00:28:45,812 --> 00:28:46,942
But the answer is still no.

456
00:28:47,012 --> 00:28:49,812
From today, I will only take elegant roles.

457
00:28:49,812 --> 00:28:50,812
Find someone else.

458
00:28:55,422 --> 00:28:56,822
To you, ma'am...

459
00:28:57,652 --> 00:28:58,992
I will be honest.

460
00:29:00,322 --> 00:29:02,392
Do not be honest. It is scary.

461
00:29:03,992 --> 00:29:06,532
I thought I would need it at least once,

462
00:29:06,592 --> 00:29:08,862
so I asked to film this first.

463
00:29:09,602 --> 00:29:10,602
Actually...

464
00:29:11,932 --> 00:29:13,332
They say I have dementia...

465
00:29:15,342 --> 00:29:17,702
I guess I am done with acting.

466
00:29:21,212 --> 00:29:22,212
Dementia?

467
00:29:22,282 --> 00:29:24,582
Yeong Ju, let me ask you for one favour.

468
00:29:24,912 --> 00:29:29,352
There is a young lady who calls me Father.

469
00:29:29,982 --> 00:29:33,522
Before all the memories disappear from my head.

470
00:29:33,922 --> 00:29:35,052
I...

471
00:29:35,262 --> 00:29:38,992
want to play the role of a good father just one more time.

472
00:29:50,102 --> 00:29:51,902
I really missed you, Stepmother...

473
00:29:52,842 --> 00:29:54,342
My foot, as if you missed me...

474
00:29:55,642 --> 00:29:57,342
What was my name in this drama?

475
00:29:57,412 --> 00:29:58,712
Man, I have played the mom role so many times...

476
00:29:58,782 --> 00:30:00,052
that I cannot remember my name at all.

477
00:30:00,882 --> 00:30:02,982
- Na Ae Jeong. - Na Ae Jeong...

478
00:30:03,052 --> 00:30:04,282
What about you two? I am your mom,

479
00:30:04,352 --> 00:30:05,652
so I should at least know my daughters' names.

480
00:30:06,352 --> 00:30:07,392
I am Yoo Se Ri.

481
00:30:08,392 --> 00:30:09,392
I am Kim Da Mi.

482
00:30:09,662 --> 00:30:10,722
Why are your last names different?

483
00:30:12,662 --> 00:30:15,902
Did I cheat in this drama? I did. I definitely did.

484
00:30:17,202 --> 00:30:18,832
I did. I definitely cheated...

485
00:30:19,472 --> 00:30:21,872
Stepmother. I found Father.

486
00:30:22,372 --> 00:30:23,972
He did not pass away.

487
00:30:25,172 --> 00:30:27,342
Right, well, you see...

488
00:30:27,412 --> 00:30:28,472
I heard he put on a whole show...

489
00:30:28,542 --> 00:30:30,212
just so you could get the insurance money.

490
00:30:30,442 --> 00:30:31,812
He is here right now.

491
00:30:41,152 --> 00:30:43,892
Sir, what is going on?

492
00:30:43,892 --> 00:30:46,662
I am that young lady's father right now.

493
00:30:46,732 --> 00:30:47,732
So you should...

494
00:30:47,792 --> 00:30:50,602
Yes. I do not know what the situation is,

495
00:30:50,662 --> 00:30:52,302
but I will do whatever you say, sir.

496
00:30:52,472 --> 00:30:55,572
Thank you, Yeong Ju. But I...

497
00:30:55,742 --> 00:30:58,912
They say my mind comes and goes now. Even this state of mind...

498
00:30:59,012 --> 00:31:01,872
- might not last very long. - Yes, yes.

499
00:31:02,142 --> 00:31:03,382
I will do as you say.

500
00:31:04,042 --> 00:31:05,042
Let us go.

501
00:31:06,412 --> 00:31:09,122
Hong Du must be happy.

502
00:31:09,182 --> 00:31:10,752
Hong Du, it is always Hong Du.

503
00:31:10,822 --> 00:31:13,552
Your father just cares about you so incredibly much.

504
00:31:16,522 --> 00:31:17,822
Have you all been well?

505
00:31:18,832 --> 00:31:19,832
Good.

506
00:31:26,472 --> 00:31:27,472
This is delicious.

507
00:31:28,372 --> 00:31:30,702
It is delicious. Really. Sorry.

508
00:31:31,242 --> 00:31:32,412
My hand slipped.

509
00:31:34,342 --> 00:31:35,512
A mistake?

510
00:31:52,632 --> 00:31:53,932
Are you that happy?

511
00:31:54,062 --> 00:31:55,932
Enough to smile so wide it makes you look ugly?

512
00:31:56,162 --> 00:31:58,972
Yes. Thank you so much, Um Tae Bong.

513
00:32:01,872 --> 00:32:03,172
This should be enough, right?

514
00:32:04,772 --> 00:32:05,772
This is delicious, delicious.

515
00:32:06,212 --> 00:32:09,742
Now, now, let us take a picture. Gather around, gather around, here.

516
00:32:09,812 --> 00:32:11,712
- Cheese. - Cheese.

517
00:32:11,782 --> 00:32:14,252
- One, two, three. - Cheese.

518
00:32:14,312 --> 00:32:16,882
Wait, ladies, it looks like you are acting.

519
00:32:19,722 --> 00:32:21,352
Your expressions are great now, they are great now.

520
00:32:21,422 --> 00:32:22,422
One, two, three.

521
00:32:49,182 --> 00:32:50,552
I should pack this too.

522
00:33:03,162 --> 00:33:04,732
Father, hold on a second.

523
00:33:09,942 --> 00:33:12,102
Here. Let us go.

524
00:33:47,772 --> 00:33:48,912
Father.

525
00:33:49,742 --> 00:33:50,882
I will visit often.

526
00:33:52,712 --> 00:33:54,452
Make sure you eat well,

527
00:33:54,612 --> 00:33:59,122
and even if it is a hassle, make sure to wash up properly.

528
00:34:00,092 --> 00:34:01,092
Okay?

529
00:34:02,092 --> 00:34:03,092
Go.

530
00:34:05,732 --> 00:34:06,732
Go.

531
00:34:08,932 --> 00:34:11,962
My beautiful daughter, our Hong Du.

532
00:34:13,202 --> 00:34:15,002
For finding your Father...

533
00:34:15,402 --> 00:34:16,572
Thank you.

534
00:34:21,772 --> 00:34:23,342
Because of me, you...

535
00:34:23,412 --> 00:34:27,282
- went through the most trouble. - No, not at all, sir.

536
00:34:27,812 --> 00:34:29,382
Please stay healthy, sir.

537
00:34:34,922 --> 00:34:35,992
Tae Bong.

538
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:41,132
Thank you for bringing me here on a day that is not too cold.

539
00:34:46,132 --> 00:34:47,332
Our Hong Du.

540
00:34:50,342 --> 00:34:51,402
Please take care of her.

541
00:34:53,742 --> 00:34:55,842
Yes, sir.

542
00:34:59,912 --> 00:35:00,912
Go.

543
00:35:01,612 --> 00:35:03,952
Go. Traffic will be bad.

544
00:35:04,952 --> 00:35:06,222
Let's go inside now.

545
00:35:06,492 --> 00:35:07,492
Go.

546
00:35:09,422 --> 00:35:10,422
Go.

547
00:35:12,762 --> 00:35:13,762
Go.

548
00:35:27,342 --> 00:35:28,442
Go.

549
00:36:46,292 --> 00:36:48,622
It must be annoying to commute for every schedule.

550
00:36:49,192 --> 00:36:51,162
Why don't you live at my house?

551
00:36:52,362 --> 00:36:53,992
Father is not here anymore anyway.

552
00:36:54,762 --> 00:36:56,962
I will come every day instead.

553
00:36:57,802 --> 00:36:59,972
All right, go on.

554
00:37:03,902 --> 00:37:05,272
Thank you for everything.

555
00:37:06,172 --> 00:37:07,872
I was truly happy because of you.

556
00:37:08,972 --> 00:37:10,812
Me, and Father too.

557
00:37:20,092 --> 00:37:21,922
Would three seconds be okay?

558
00:37:22,492 --> 00:37:23,492
What?

559
00:37:33,772 --> 00:37:34,772
Hey...

560
00:37:34,832 --> 00:37:36,642
What did you just do?

561
00:37:38,372 --> 00:37:39,512
I mean...

562
00:37:39,742 --> 00:37:42,382
- You just... - You are still fine?

563
00:37:42,482 --> 00:37:44,282
Is it really okay because it was three seconds?

564
00:37:48,282 --> 00:37:49,982
I guess you really are okay?

565
00:37:50,882 --> 00:37:52,282
I guess so.

566
00:37:52,352 --> 00:37:53,692
Nothing to be scared of, Um Tae Bong.

567
00:37:53,752 --> 00:37:55,192
You really were okay with three seconds...

568
00:38:42,942 --> 00:38:45,102
Three seconds have passed!

569
00:38:45,202 --> 00:38:46,442
No, it feels like a full minute!

570
00:38:47,572 --> 00:38:49,712
I'm going to faint.

571
00:38:50,112 --> 00:38:52,752
So I can't take you home. You can go by yourself, right?

572
00:38:53,382 --> 00:38:54,452
I am fainting.

573
00:39:02,152 --> 00:39:04,762
I will faint soon, right? I am going to faint...

574
00:39:04,892 --> 00:39:07,492
I'm fainting now. Four.

575
00:39:07,692 --> 00:39:10,302
Making a soft spot to faint on. Three.

576
00:39:11,202 --> 00:39:15,172
I'm lying down now. Two. I'm fainting.

577
00:39:15,432 --> 00:39:16,442
One.

578
00:39:25,142 --> 00:39:26,152
Should I try again?

579
00:39:26,852 --> 00:39:27,852
One.

580
00:39:30,982 --> 00:39:31,982
What?

581
00:40:08,352 --> 00:40:09,862
She left by herself.

582
00:40:13,532 --> 00:40:14,792
Cha Hong Du.

583
00:40:15,692 --> 00:40:17,002
I guess I am okay now.

584
00:40:18,302 --> 00:40:21,802
But why did I really get better?

585
00:40:27,942 --> 00:40:28,972
It is Mr. Han.

586
00:40:30,182 --> 00:40:31,582
Are you really back now?

587
00:40:34,282 --> 00:40:35,652
So this is what you looked like.

588
00:40:36,822 --> 00:40:38,082
I really wanted to meet you.

589
00:40:39,352 --> 00:40:42,252
So I really cannot let you go anymore.

590
00:40:47,932 --> 00:40:49,632
That's all I'm saying.

591
00:40:52,262 --> 00:40:55,502
I am really home.

592
00:40:56,102 --> 00:40:58,672
Our penthouse, the best in the world.

593
00:41:15,192 --> 00:41:17,092
I think it is time to answer...

594
00:41:17,862 --> 00:41:19,292
why you're so interested in the owner's family.

595
00:41:19,892 --> 00:41:21,962
I met an old gentleman in London.

596
00:41:22,932 --> 00:41:25,002
His granddaughter was struggling with emotional pain,

597
00:41:25,302 --> 00:41:27,902
and he asked if I'd be her friend if we ever met.

598
00:41:29,202 --> 00:41:30,272
I only found out who that man was...

599
00:41:31,342 --> 00:41:33,072
after we parted ways.

600
00:41:34,472 --> 00:41:35,472
Chairman Wang?

601
00:41:35,772 --> 00:41:36,782
Yes.

602
00:41:38,182 --> 00:41:40,652
I did some background checks too.

603
00:41:41,212 --> 00:41:43,322
Director Han Jung Woo signed the contract for this place...

604
00:41:43,482 --> 00:41:44,752
regardless of the young lady.

605
00:41:44,822 --> 00:41:46,422
He was quite a troublemaker in London.

606
00:41:46,522 --> 00:41:48,952
He couldn't just walk past friends who were being bullied.

607
00:41:49,392 --> 00:41:51,792
Could you do the same for the young lady?

608
00:41:52,262 --> 00:41:54,632
Cha Hong Du is a character from a drama...

609
00:41:54,692 --> 00:41:55,962
that Um Tae Bong starred in.

610
00:41:56,802 --> 00:41:59,602
- Does Um Tae Bong know? - He probably didn't know at first,

611
00:42:00,172 --> 00:42:03,602
- but yes, he knows now. - And?

612
00:42:03,672 --> 00:42:05,502
He's putting on an act for the young lady.

613
00:42:06,312 --> 00:42:07,372
And even now,

614
00:42:07,442 --> 00:42:09,742
he still doesn't know the young lady's true identity.

615
00:42:12,342 --> 00:42:13,352
No. Why on earth...

616
00:42:14,652 --> 00:42:16,322
did Oh Hae Ra abandon her true self?

617
00:42:17,052 --> 00:42:19,152
She'll return to her old self someday.

618
00:42:19,792 --> 00:42:22,892
If you truly care about the young lady, I have a favour to ask.

619
00:42:23,122 --> 00:42:24,892
Right now, in the world she's living in,

620
00:42:24,962 --> 00:42:28,562
so she can be a little happier, please just watch over her.

621
00:42:29,262 --> 00:42:32,002
Manager Nam Goong, what does Oh Hae Ra like most?

622
00:42:33,372 --> 00:42:35,132
Something that has absolutely nothing to do with Um Tae Bong...

623
00:42:42,842 --> 00:42:45,842
Wow, it's my favourite tent.

624
00:42:50,152 --> 00:42:52,382
You must be a total pro.

625
00:42:52,382 --> 00:42:54,022
Whoever Mr. Han ends up dating later...

626
00:42:54,092 --> 00:42:57,462
- is going to be so lucky. - Later?

627
00:42:59,762 --> 00:43:04,432
I mean, you'll meet a wonderful woman someday.

628
00:43:10,102 --> 00:43:11,402
What's the best part of camping?

629
00:43:13,272 --> 00:43:14,272
Meat?

630
00:43:16,882 --> 00:43:17,882
Here.

631
00:43:19,342 --> 00:43:23,022
I smell someone burning meat from a mile away.

632
00:43:38,802 --> 00:43:41,702
I completely forgot that director lives right next door.

633
00:43:42,232 --> 00:43:43,672
This is very dangerous.

634
00:43:44,842 --> 00:43:45,942
At this rate,

635
00:43:46,412 --> 00:43:48,972
she'll see traces of me every time she opens her eyes.

636
00:43:49,042 --> 00:43:50,442
Even when I'm not there,

637
00:43:50,642 --> 00:43:52,412
it'll feel like I'm there every single second.

638
00:43:56,122 --> 00:43:57,122
What's this?

639
00:43:58,652 --> 00:43:59,852
Why aren't you coming out?

640
00:44:01,592 --> 00:44:03,992
What are you doing without the owner's permission?

641
00:44:04,492 --> 00:44:07,262
Hey, why so serious...

642
00:44:11,002 --> 00:44:13,402
I didn't look, I didn't look, I didn't see anything.

643
00:44:14,232 --> 00:44:16,472
Whatever. Just hurry up and come out...

644
00:44:16,542 --> 00:44:19,472
before I eat it all. Come out, come out!

645
00:44:19,612 --> 00:44:21,272
Underwear?

646
00:44:25,582 --> 00:44:27,482
Hong Du, try this.

647
00:44:32,422 --> 00:44:33,452
Is this really Korean beef?

648
00:44:33,592 --> 00:44:36,092
If it's not top-grade premium Korean beef,

649
00:44:36,092 --> 00:44:37,092
I won't even touch...

650
00:44:42,432 --> 00:44:44,332
Mr. Han, you should eat while you cook.

651
00:44:48,132 --> 00:44:51,472
It's so tender and delicious. Grill it a bit faster.

652
00:44:51,772 --> 00:44:53,312
Are you always this slow?

653
00:44:57,282 --> 00:44:58,882
Are you trying to shove a whole cow in your mouth?

654
00:44:59,612 --> 00:45:01,212
Do you think I'm eating this because it's good?

655
00:45:01,352 --> 00:45:03,782
I'm just forcing it down so we don't have any food waste.

656
00:45:03,852 --> 00:45:05,652
Do you know how much I care about the environment...

657
00:45:05,722 --> 00:45:08,022
Hong Du, don't pay attention to him and try this.

658
00:45:11,962 --> 00:45:13,892
You two are really teaming up to cut me off.

659
00:45:13,992 --> 00:45:15,592
Very clever.

660
00:45:15,832 --> 00:45:17,862
Mr. Han prepared everything for this camping trip today,

661
00:45:17,932 --> 00:45:19,062
and you came empty-handed.

662
00:45:19,162 --> 00:45:20,632
Empty-handed? What do you mean, empty-handed?

663
00:45:20,932 --> 00:45:22,432
I brought the best gift of all.

664
00:45:23,142 --> 00:45:24,142
That.

665
00:45:30,342 --> 00:45:32,142
Why do you think it's a life-size cutout?

666
00:45:32,212 --> 00:45:34,052
Because it shines brightly like a lighthouse,

667
00:45:34,112 --> 00:45:35,182
that's why it's a life-size cutout.

668
00:45:35,382 --> 00:45:38,652
See? Just with that one thing, the whole neighbourhood is bright.

669
00:45:39,792 --> 00:45:41,152
Bright, my foot.

670
00:45:41,252 --> 00:45:42,792
It looks like it is going to rain any minute.

671
00:45:42,892 --> 00:45:45,322
Anyone who brings their own face as a gift to someone's house...

672
00:45:45,392 --> 00:45:48,162
is just a life-size idiot, isn't that what it really means?

673
00:45:50,802 --> 00:45:53,702
It is okay, I prepared a gift for Tae Bong.

674
00:45:54,032 --> 00:45:55,632
A gift? What kind of gift?

675
00:45:56,842 --> 00:45:58,702
The gift should be arriving right about now.

676
00:46:01,572 --> 00:46:02,572
There.

677
00:46:18,592 --> 00:46:21,532
You guys are so mean, leaving me out like this.

678
00:46:23,902 --> 00:46:26,772
You... Why are you...

679
00:46:31,602 --> 00:46:32,972
Here we go.

680
00:46:33,772 --> 00:46:36,542
- All right, ask your question. - All right, then, Song Na Ri,

681
00:46:36,612 --> 00:46:39,082
here is your Truth or Dare question.

682
00:46:39,142 --> 00:46:40,152
Okay.

683
00:46:40,712 --> 00:46:42,912
Right here, right now,

684
00:46:43,882 --> 00:46:46,492
is there someone you like? Yes or no?

685
00:46:46,552 --> 00:46:49,322
Look at how childish that question is.

686
00:46:49,962 --> 00:46:52,192
Before that, I have something to reveal.

687
00:46:53,132 --> 00:46:56,092
- Our contract relationship... - Yes, there is.

688
00:47:00,202 --> 00:47:02,132
I like that person a lot.

689
00:47:09,912 --> 00:47:10,912
Now it is my turn.

690
00:47:15,312 --> 00:47:18,122
You, what should I ask you?

691
00:47:19,722 --> 00:47:20,822
When was your last kiss?

692
00:47:21,352 --> 00:47:24,562
The one at the party that day does not count as a kiss.

693
00:47:27,162 --> 00:47:30,502
I know everything. The agency set that whole thing up.

694
00:47:30,632 --> 00:47:32,762
To keep Tae Bong's mysterious image going.

695
00:47:33,232 --> 00:47:35,472
Not that one, a real kiss.

696
00:47:36,672 --> 00:47:38,842
Well.

697
00:47:39,872 --> 00:47:40,972
That was...

698
00:47:42,072 --> 00:47:43,082
Yesterday?

699
00:47:44,242 --> 00:47:45,242
Yesterday?

700
00:47:51,782 --> 00:47:52,782
It is my turn, right?

701
00:48:01,332 --> 00:48:03,502
Oh, right. At the beach,

702
00:48:03,702 --> 00:48:05,962
the night we went to find the ring, what you said to me.

703
00:48:06,532 --> 00:48:07,632
You are not Cha Hong Du.

704
00:48:08,132 --> 00:48:11,742
Your name and the world you believe in. None of it is real.

705
00:48:12,342 --> 00:48:15,142
That has been bothering me.

706
00:48:16,112 --> 00:48:17,582
Someday, are you going to tell me...

707
00:48:18,412 --> 00:48:19,752
the real reason why you said that?

708
00:48:23,382 --> 00:48:25,082
What is it? Are you two sharing secrets?

709
00:48:25,452 --> 00:48:28,122
Drink up, drink up!

710
00:48:28,192 --> 00:48:30,022
How long are you going to make me dance?

711
00:48:30,092 --> 00:48:31,662
Look at my shoulders! They're dislocated!

712
00:48:31,722 --> 00:48:33,992
Dislocated, dislocated!

713
00:48:34,292 --> 00:48:35,292
Darn it.

714
00:48:38,032 --> 00:48:39,362
Hong Du, are you okay?

715
00:48:39,432 --> 00:48:41,072
Is this not your first time drinking?

716
00:48:41,702 --> 00:48:42,902
Dong Seok told me...

717
00:48:43,472 --> 00:48:45,242
that this guy isn't allowed to have even a single drink.

718
00:48:46,272 --> 00:48:47,972
Anyway, so this is what soju tastes like.

719
00:48:48,542 --> 00:48:50,282
It is really bitter...

720
00:48:51,612 --> 00:48:52,612
and sweet.

721
00:48:57,452 --> 00:48:58,452
My turn.

722
00:49:09,062 --> 00:49:10,062
Someday...

723
00:49:11,932 --> 00:49:13,132
No matter what I say...

724
00:49:15,372 --> 00:49:16,572
That it was all for you...

725
00:49:18,872 --> 00:49:19,912
Will you believe me?

726
00:49:28,212 --> 00:49:30,782
Yes, of course.

727
00:49:44,062 --> 00:49:48,032
Why is it so cramped? Help me up, hey.

728
00:49:50,802 --> 00:49:53,872
Why is it so cold? Why is this floor so hard?

729
00:49:53,942 --> 00:49:55,442
I can't sleep in a place like this, gosh.

730
00:49:55,942 --> 00:49:57,642
And yet you brought a sleeping bag?

731
00:49:57,712 --> 00:50:01,382
- I am always thoroughly prepared. - You always have an excuse.

732
00:50:03,452 --> 00:50:06,592
Hey, won't you come work as my bodyguard?

733
00:50:06,992 --> 00:50:08,352
Even if I offer you the best compensation?

734
00:50:08,892 --> 00:50:09,892
I...

735
00:50:10,962 --> 00:50:12,362
have to stay by Um Tae Bong's side.

736
00:50:14,932 --> 00:50:17,562
I think I'm catching a cold.

737
00:50:18,262 --> 00:50:19,562
Who told you to sleep here?

738
00:50:19,662 --> 00:50:20,932
I am telling you to go home right now.

739
00:50:21,002 --> 00:50:22,472
No, I am not going.

740
00:50:25,102 --> 00:50:26,972
Why is this tent so small?

741
00:50:29,312 --> 00:50:32,112
Are you not cold? Why do you not just go home?

742
00:50:35,152 --> 00:50:36,452
This is nothing.

743
00:50:36,952 --> 00:50:38,722
You must have seen Korean variety shows.

744
00:50:39,082 --> 00:50:41,392
Sleeping outside in the cold is a piece of cake for us.

745
00:50:42,952 --> 00:50:45,162
You must be freezing, right?

746
00:50:46,892 --> 00:50:47,892
Not at all.

747
00:50:48,592 --> 00:50:49,592
What do you know?

748
00:50:49,662 --> 00:50:51,432
About winter in London? You have no idea.

749
00:50:51,502 --> 00:50:52,862
Wow, acting tough.

750
00:50:58,742 --> 00:51:01,812
Do you have any extra heat packs, by the way?

751
00:51:03,782 --> 00:51:06,752
No, but you bought a lot earlier. You grabbed a bunch of them.

752
00:51:07,712 --> 00:51:09,582
I gave them all to the ladies in case they were cold.

753
00:51:10,482 --> 00:51:11,522
All of them?

754
00:51:13,352 --> 00:51:15,052
You acted tough in front of the women.

755
00:51:15,122 --> 00:51:18,992
And now you are acting weak? Are you always this two-faced?

756
00:51:19,692 --> 00:51:20,762
You are not even going to give me one,

757
00:51:20,832 --> 00:51:21,862
yet you talk so much.

758
00:51:22,932 --> 00:51:24,202
Just go home already.

759
00:51:25,062 --> 00:51:26,972
Do you own this entire rooftop?

760
00:51:27,632 --> 00:51:30,972
Move over a bit. You are so selfish.

761
00:51:31,342 --> 00:51:34,212
Do you want me to show you what selfish really is?

762
00:51:35,872 --> 00:51:36,882
Gosh.

763
00:51:40,252 --> 00:51:41,782
Move away, please.

764
00:52:05,542 --> 00:52:07,242
Why? Can you not sleep?

765
00:52:08,342 --> 00:52:09,342
What about you?

766
00:52:10,482 --> 00:52:12,442
Someone is snoring too loudly.

767
00:52:15,412 --> 00:52:16,622
Are you glad to be back?

768
00:52:18,522 --> 00:52:20,892
Yes. I think I have...

769
00:52:21,492 --> 00:52:22,992
finally become a real adult.

770
00:52:24,422 --> 00:52:25,762
I act strong,

771
00:52:26,732 --> 00:52:28,292
but I was actually terrified of living.

772
00:52:30,132 --> 00:52:33,232
But now, I think I will be fine even on my own.

773
00:52:35,572 --> 00:52:36,672
So you insist on...

774
00:52:36,672 --> 00:52:39,702
- living here all alone? - Yes.

775
00:52:40,612 --> 00:52:43,212
I think I have grown a lot recently.

776
00:52:45,782 --> 00:52:46,782
It is all thanks to you.

777
00:52:48,452 --> 00:52:49,452
Thank you.

778
00:52:55,092 --> 00:52:57,462
Oh, right. Yesterday,

779
00:52:59,622 --> 00:53:01,132
after you kissed me and left,

780
00:53:03,432 --> 00:53:04,462
I did not faint.

781
00:53:05,402 --> 00:53:06,462
Really?

782
00:53:08,572 --> 00:53:09,572
I think...

783
00:53:11,042 --> 00:53:12,042
I am cured.

784
00:53:13,742 --> 00:53:14,742
Thank you, too.

785
00:53:16,642 --> 00:53:17,642
That's a relief.

786
00:54:07,792 --> 00:54:10,162
Are you the lazy type?

787
00:54:10,402 --> 00:54:12,962
The person who slept in should clean everything up.

788
00:54:26,712 --> 00:54:27,712
Hey.

789
00:54:30,752 --> 00:54:32,552
You said you couldn't sleep in a new bed,

790
00:54:32,622 --> 00:54:34,192
but it sounded like a tank drove by all night.

791
00:54:34,252 --> 00:54:36,122
Gosh, did you two disappear together again?

792
00:54:40,432 --> 00:54:41,432
My stomach is killing me.

793
00:54:44,402 --> 00:54:45,962
How much did I drink yesterday?

794
00:54:46,662 --> 00:54:47,832
My head is going to split open.

795
00:54:48,172 --> 00:54:49,902
You were chugging straight from the bottle yesterday.

796
00:54:49,972 --> 00:54:51,842
As an idol, I guess you live on spirits.

797
00:54:52,442 --> 00:54:53,512
Is that supposed to be a joke?

798
00:54:53,742 --> 00:54:55,742
When is the food coming out?

799
00:54:56,812 --> 00:54:59,212
- Thank you. - Thank you.

800
00:54:59,612 --> 00:55:00,982
- It's hot. - I'm sorry.

801
00:55:06,052 --> 00:55:07,992
My mom always told me that when it comes to meat broth,

802
00:55:08,052 --> 00:55:09,592
I shouldn't waste a single drop.

803
00:55:10,622 --> 00:55:12,092
Shall I dig in?

804
00:55:19,002 --> 00:55:20,062
(Blood Sausage Soup Restaurant)

805
00:55:23,842 --> 00:55:24,842
What?

806
00:55:25,172 --> 00:55:26,172
Have you never seen a female celebrity...

807
00:55:26,242 --> 00:55:27,242
shake a bowl of rice?

808
00:55:28,512 --> 00:55:29,512
No.

809
00:55:30,542 --> 00:55:31,542
Unbelievable.

810
00:55:38,846 --> 00:55:41,686
Hot soup is definitely the best hangover cure.

811
00:55:43,556 --> 00:55:44,826
If you aren't going to eat that, I will.

812
00:55:44,886 --> 00:55:45,886
No, go ahead and eat.

813
00:55:53,396 --> 00:55:54,466
But I feel a bit sorry.

814
00:55:55,396 --> 00:55:58,036
I think I confused you with someone else.

815
00:56:00,106 --> 00:56:02,136
If they look like me, did we see the same surgeon?

816
00:56:04,646 --> 00:56:05,706
I didn't get plastic surgery.

817
00:56:05,946 --> 00:56:07,776
I only had my eyes done a little, that's all.

818
00:56:07,846 --> 00:56:11,116
You can't tell, right? It looks natural.

819
00:56:14,886 --> 00:56:15,886
Na Ri...

820
00:56:16,986 --> 00:56:18,756
The more I see you, the more I think you're a really good person.

821
00:56:25,696 --> 00:56:26,696
I'm just saying.

822
00:56:30,906 --> 00:56:31,906
It's hot.

823
00:56:34,876 --> 00:56:36,536
Wait, are you going to bring that to Cha Hong Du?

824
00:56:36,636 --> 00:56:38,246
They already ran off together earlier anyway.

825
00:56:38,876 --> 00:56:40,676
They might be back by now.

826
00:56:41,476 --> 00:56:42,876
I should give it to her quickly before it gets cold.

827
00:56:43,076 --> 00:56:45,546
You're so devoted, aren't you?

828
00:56:46,346 --> 00:56:48,316
Look who it is.

829
00:56:50,086 --> 00:56:51,126
Song Na Ri.

830
00:56:52,326 --> 00:56:54,596
Our former jewellery model.

831
00:56:54,856 --> 00:56:57,226
That day, because of that rude jerk Um Tae Bong,

832
00:56:57,426 --> 00:56:58,666
my mood was completely ruined.

833
00:56:58,726 --> 00:57:00,536
I heard your relationship with Um Tae Bong was fake.

834
00:57:01,596 --> 00:57:02,866
We should get a drink sometime.

835
00:57:03,166 --> 00:57:05,236
You can tell me some fun stories about the entertainment industry.

836
00:57:06,836 --> 00:57:08,006
And we can renew your modelling contract.

837
00:57:09,406 --> 00:57:11,276
Why isn't he helping me when this guy is talking like this?

838
00:57:12,146 --> 00:57:14,446
Your new manager? He has a good attitude.

839
00:57:14,646 --> 00:57:16,676
He doesn't interrupt and ruin the mood like someone else.

840
00:57:17,346 --> 00:57:20,486
So, let's make some time soon.

841
00:57:26,326 --> 00:57:29,796
Why are you just sitting there? That guy was hitting on me,

842
00:57:29,856 --> 00:57:31,296
so why didn't you help me?

843
00:57:33,426 --> 00:57:34,496
Song Na Ri, are you a child?

844
00:57:35,736 --> 00:57:37,106
Can't you handle something like this yourself?

845
00:57:37,966 --> 00:57:40,536
All you have to say is yes or no, so why couldn't you say anything?

846
00:57:46,576 --> 00:57:47,646
You can go home by yourself, right?

847
00:57:49,016 --> 00:57:50,016
You aren't a child.

848
00:58:01,456 --> 00:58:02,456
This is good.

849
00:58:02,696 --> 00:58:05,696
We were also looking for a reliable businessman like you, sir.

850
00:58:06,496 --> 00:58:07,566
Thank you.

851
00:58:09,036 --> 00:58:11,336
CEO, so this is where you were. You did not go far.

852
00:58:12,506 --> 00:58:13,506
Excuse me, who is this?

853
00:58:14,376 --> 00:58:16,176
What does the manager from earlier want?

854
00:58:16,606 --> 00:58:18,446
CEO, about what you mentioned earlier,

855
00:58:18,506 --> 00:58:19,546
the sponsorship.

856
00:58:19,946 --> 00:58:20,946
What?

857
00:58:21,276 --> 00:58:23,446
- Hello. - Hello.

858
00:58:23,516 --> 00:58:25,216
Do you not think Song Na Ri is the wrong choice?

859
00:58:25,686 --> 00:58:27,986
- What? - If you are going to do it,

860
00:58:28,116 --> 00:58:29,556
you should help someone who is struggling.

861
00:58:29,856 --> 00:58:33,256
You are a married man, so why did you take off your ring?

862
00:58:33,726 --> 00:58:35,296
It has not been long since you were released from prison...

863
00:58:35,356 --> 00:58:36,356
because of a woman.

864
00:58:36,426 --> 00:58:38,096
How much longer will you keep asking for sponsorships?

865
00:58:38,166 --> 00:58:39,666
Hold on.

866
00:58:39,896 --> 00:58:42,766
- CEO Kim, is this who you are? - No, well...

867
00:58:42,836 --> 00:58:44,936
Let us pretend this investment talk never happened.

868
00:58:45,506 --> 00:58:47,706
No...

869
00:58:50,806 --> 00:58:52,406
Hey, who do you think you are, punk.

870
00:58:55,216 --> 00:58:56,946
Let us just say I am Song Na Ri's male friend.

871
00:58:57,716 --> 00:58:58,946
Or maybe something more.

872
00:59:03,216 --> 00:59:04,386
Hey!

873
00:59:08,296 --> 00:59:09,526
(Han Jung Woo)

874
00:59:12,866 --> 00:59:13,936
Are you not going to answer?

875
00:59:14,966 --> 00:59:15,966
No, I am not.

876
00:59:16,866 --> 00:59:19,506
- Do you even know who it is? - I am not answering because I know.

877
00:59:22,206 --> 00:59:23,236
(Han Jung Woo)

878
00:59:25,306 --> 00:59:29,076
(Never Answering)

879
00:59:33,586 --> 00:59:36,086
Song Na Ri is upset, she is really upset.

880
00:59:43,426 --> 00:59:45,096
The hangover soup is getting cold,

881
00:59:45,166 --> 00:59:46,766
and the person who is supposed to eat it is not here.

882
00:59:48,596 --> 00:59:50,266
Looks like our oath of brotherhood is broken again.

883
00:59:56,336 --> 00:59:59,076
Can you photoshop my face in there? Make it look natural.

884
00:59:59,146 --> 01:00:02,016
- Excuse me? - I am his cousin.

885
01:00:02,276 --> 01:00:03,786
And that is our family photo.

886
01:00:04,516 --> 01:00:05,786
A family photo?

887
01:00:06,446 --> 01:00:07,716
These people are all stars...

888
01:00:07,786 --> 01:00:09,516
Star students. Make us look classy, you know?

889
01:00:10,116 --> 01:00:11,626
Classy, you know?

890
01:00:13,126 --> 01:00:14,696
Yes, understood.

891
01:00:17,196 --> 01:00:19,766
Is this what you wanted to do first thing in the morning?

892
01:00:19,826 --> 01:00:22,336
Yes, because you are the only one missing from the photo.

893
01:00:22,596 --> 01:00:24,666
Thanks to you, I found my whole family.

894
01:00:25,536 --> 01:00:28,706
I thought it would be nice if you were in this photo too.

895
01:00:33,846 --> 01:00:35,576
Cha Hong Du, I am sorry.

896
01:00:36,546 --> 01:00:37,586
This is all fake.

897
01:00:43,616 --> 01:00:46,326
I love it so much.

898
01:00:46,826 --> 01:00:49,726
All my wishes have come true now. You made them all happen.

899
01:00:55,596 --> 01:00:57,936
No. There is one more left.

900
01:00:58,466 --> 01:01:00,606
If I am going down the wrong path...

901
01:01:00,676 --> 01:01:02,836
But I keep going without realising it.

902
01:01:02,906 --> 01:01:06,246
Then you have to appear right in front of me,

903
01:01:08,876 --> 01:01:10,916
so I can return to where I belong.

904
01:01:12,886 --> 01:01:14,386
I want you to do that for me too.

905
01:01:17,556 --> 01:01:19,126
Now I will find the real you.

906
01:01:19,756 --> 01:01:20,756
That is...

907
01:01:21,396 --> 01:01:23,556
the last thing I will do for you.

908
01:01:31,606 --> 01:01:32,906
I will get going. Take care.

909
01:01:33,536 --> 01:01:34,536
Wait a minute.

910
01:01:35,936 --> 01:01:37,146
Later at nine o'clock...

911
01:01:38,046 --> 01:01:39,046
come over to my house.

912
01:01:39,946 --> 01:01:41,516
I really have something to tell you.

913
01:01:42,446 --> 01:01:43,446
You can just tell me now.

914
01:01:44,016 --> 01:01:45,086
No, later.

915
01:01:45,946 --> 01:01:46,946
At nine.

916
01:01:48,116 --> 01:01:49,416
Got it. See you later.

917
01:01:49,956 --> 01:01:53,026
(Jubong Sweet and Spicy Fried Chicken)

918
01:01:56,496 --> 01:01:58,396
I am doing the right thing, right?

919
01:02:14,246 --> 01:02:17,016
A few days ago, when you went out to take out the trash,

920
01:02:17,076 --> 01:02:18,086
where did you go?

921
01:02:18,586 --> 01:02:19,586
Did you meet someone?

922
01:02:20,416 --> 01:02:21,416
No.

923
01:02:22,156 --> 01:02:23,156
I did not meet anyone.

924
01:02:25,826 --> 01:02:27,456
Why do you not go visit Tae Bong?

925
01:02:27,526 --> 01:02:28,796
I packed some side dishes for you to give him.

926
01:02:30,766 --> 01:02:33,096
You can go to his house anytime now.

927
01:02:35,436 --> 01:02:36,436
Now?

928
01:02:36,736 --> 01:02:38,966
At the charity event, I heard Tae Bong...

929
01:02:39,106 --> 01:02:40,266
and Hong Du had something going on.

930
01:02:40,906 --> 01:02:42,206
CEO Park probably ordered them to do that.

931
01:02:42,506 --> 01:02:44,476
That punk Tae Bong might be easily swayed,

932
01:02:45,776 --> 01:02:47,046
but he will never forget his first love.

933
01:03:03,426 --> 01:03:05,526
Mr. Han, thank you for the camping.

934
01:03:06,026 --> 01:03:07,596
I will never forget it for the rest of my life.

935
01:03:09,266 --> 01:03:11,806
What exactly did the heiress go through...

936
01:03:11,866 --> 01:03:13,236
It was not in the newspapers,

937
01:03:14,176 --> 01:03:15,706
but there was a kidnapping incident that day.

938
01:03:21,076 --> 01:03:22,076
Could that be...

939
01:03:23,746 --> 01:03:25,216
your trauma?

940
01:03:26,186 --> 01:03:28,056
Excuse me, sir. Just one more thing.

941
01:03:28,856 --> 01:03:31,986
About the car doll keychain that was found there at the time...

942
01:03:31,986 --> 01:03:33,056
Not really.

943
01:03:33,326 --> 01:03:35,396
Only a kid carries things like that around.

944
01:03:40,896 --> 01:03:42,936
Then were you there at that time?

945
01:03:43,666 --> 01:03:46,266
And you became Cha Hong Du to forget about it.

946
01:03:47,006 --> 01:03:50,536
If Um Tae Bong ends this act all of a sudden...

947
01:03:50,776 --> 01:03:54,846
(Han Jung Woo)

948
01:03:59,546 --> 01:04:00,816
Can we meet right now?

949
01:04:02,556 --> 01:04:04,126
We will get attached if we see each other often.

950
01:04:04,756 --> 01:04:06,826
I cannot go outside right now anyway.

951
01:04:16,266 --> 01:04:19,036
Manager Na, please find Um Tae Bong's address.

952
01:04:19,236 --> 01:04:20,266
Yes.

953
01:04:31,016 --> 01:04:32,846
Yes, I am almost there.

954
01:04:37,426 --> 01:04:38,656
Why did he tell me to come earlier?

955
01:04:41,456 --> 01:04:43,356
He better not make fun of me for dressing up like this.

956
01:04:54,776 --> 01:04:59,606
What is this? When did he even prepare this?

957
01:05:11,086 --> 01:05:12,626
I forgot Father's book.

958
01:05:13,856 --> 01:05:16,696
I will have to bring it to him next time.

959
01:05:27,536 --> 01:05:29,276
Hong Du, Cha Hong Du.

960
01:05:30,806 --> 01:05:32,606
(The Crown Prince's Bodyguard)

961
01:05:32,746 --> 01:05:33,976
You're fine with just tteokbokki?

962
01:05:34,616 --> 01:05:37,176
- Even though you saved me. - Yes, it is plenty.

963
01:05:37,176 --> 01:05:38,186
What is that?

964
01:05:44,656 --> 01:05:47,156
- Hong Du. - That is my story.

965
01:05:47,626 --> 01:05:49,156
How is that...

966
01:05:52,366 --> 01:05:54,896
- Why is Song Na Ri using my name... - Because that is the real one.

967
01:06:00,366 --> 01:06:01,376
And you are a fake.

968
01:06:03,636 --> 01:06:05,806
- Excuse me? - Is it that good?

969
01:06:07,076 --> 01:06:08,246
Good enough to eat while crying?

970
01:06:08,776 --> 01:06:09,776
Father?

971
01:06:09,846 --> 01:06:11,386
I love tteokbokki more than anything in the world.

972
01:06:11,446 --> 01:06:12,446
Do you understand now?

973
01:06:13,016 --> 01:06:14,956
Ms. Cha Hong Du, or rather...

974
01:06:17,016 --> 01:06:18,926
Your real name is not even Cha Hong Du, is it?

975
01:06:19,686 --> 01:06:20,686
What?

976
01:06:21,856 --> 01:06:22,856
What do you...

977
01:06:33,436 --> 01:06:34,806
What does all of that mean?

978
01:06:38,576 --> 01:06:39,576
I...

979
01:06:42,516 --> 01:06:43,616
Why am I...

980
01:06:44,546 --> 01:06:45,546
a fake?

981
01:06:49,086 --> 01:06:51,286
(The Crown Prince's Bodyguard)

982
01:07:04,936 --> 01:07:07,006
(Oh! My Guard)
